# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The site currently runs in SMS FORM SIMULATION MODE: the opt-in and opt-out
# forms reproduce the finished customer experience in the browser, but no data
# is transmitted or stored. See the comment block at the top of
# /assets/js/sms-forms.js and the "Current status" section of README.md.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy below enforces that at the browser level:
#   connect-src 'none'  -> the page cannot make any network request (no fetch/XHR),
#                          so a phone number physically cannot leave the browser.
#   form-action 'none'  -> no form can POST anywhere.
#
# WHEN THE BACKEND IS ADDED: change connect-src to 'self' so the opt-in and
# opt-out handlers in /assets/js/sms-forms.js can call the API.

# CACHING — read this before changing an asset.
#
# A stale cached stylesheet/script is not cosmetic here: new HTML served with an
# old sms-forms.js means the tab strip never appears and the submit button does
# nothing. That happened in production once already.
#
# Two defences, use BOTH:
#   1. The <link>/<script> tags carry a ?v=N query. BUMP N IN ALL THREE HTML
#      FILES whenever site.css or sms-forms.js changes. A new URL cannot be
#      served from an old cache entry.
#   2. The headers below: HTML always revalidates, so a browser can never keep
#      showing old markup pointing at old asset URLs; assets are capped at
#      10 minutes, so even a forgotten version bump self-heals quickly.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600
